  Auto mode can't check actions in this session

  Auto mode's safety check runs on the server. Your requests go through api.example.com, and the check isn't getting through.

  You can stay in auto mode and approve each action that needs the check yourself.

  Or you can leave for accept edits mode, which has no safety check, and auto mode stays off. These then run without asking: file edits
  and commands such as rm and mv in your working folders, some tools, such as subagents and scheduled tasks, and anything allowed by rules
  that auto mode set aside, such as Bash(*). This turn stops, so its waiting actions don't run, but background tasks go on. Claude goes
  on at your next message, or sooner.

  To get the check back, ask whoever runs your gateway to pass it through:
  https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permission-modes#server-side-classifier-review

  Enter to stay in auto mode · shift+Tab to leave for accept edits mode and stop · Esc to cancel
